  "_comment": "Example `<workdir>/crustify/artifacts/modules.json` (REPO-ROOT tier), emitted by the planner. A module is one translation unit with the headers it defines its items in, named by the TU's path; a header that implements what no TU does is a header module, named by its own path, with a null `translation_unit`. Every file is an entry whose `items` lists are empty when the module owns the file whole, `included` when it owns only the entities named, and `excluded` when it owns all others: here the shared include/openssl/crypto.h is split item by item among the modules that implement what it declares, and crypto/o_str.c, which mixes string lifecycle routines with other code, is split into a foundational module and another that share its name. `tests` lists the test files tied to a module, those whose subject it is: whose assertions check its results or effects, or that use its internals; a test file is listed by every module it is tied to, and its `items` select test functions. Each link unit's and module's `index` is its permanent number, not its position; dependency records name a module by its `name` and `foundational`, which tell apart the two modules of the split crypto/o_str.c. `depends_on` holds every dependency, in-tree modules and out-of-tree libraries, with its edge counts and what is consumed; statem and rec_layer_s3 depend on each other, as their `incoming_edges` show. The order of the modules, and the dependencies it cuts, are in `schedule.json`. `status` is `todo` while the plan may change and `frozen` once final. `objective` is `port` in this port campaign, but for the foundational modules, which are `wrap` in every campaign; a module's `rust_equivalent`, and each link unit's, record the closest the standard library comes to it and the crates that could replace it outright, each with its feature parity; an out-of-tree record names the library and counts what the module consumes, and dependencies.json records the library itself. The waves are in `schedule.json`. The Rust tree mirrors this decomposition; there is no second placement document. Every path is below the C root, the repository's c/.",
