 "quality_assessment": "Fit for sockets, name resolution and polling; nix is recommended there, as it covers the other areas too. Coverage: Sockets only. Socket::new sets SOCK_CLOEXEC (socket.rs:744-), connect_timeout does a non-blocking connect, poll and SO_ERROR as socket.c does (socket.rs:215, sys/unix.rs:973), and it has set_tcp_keepalive(TcpKeepalive with_time/with_interval/with_retries), take_error, send/recv and set_nonblocking. Lacks getaddrinfo/gai_strerror and inet_pton (std::net covers them) and a general poll: its send/recv timeouts are SO_SNDTIMEO/SO_RCVTIMEO, where socket.c polls on EAGAIN. Shared state: It exposes the state it holds to C (raw descriptors or handles). Soundness (sound): 215 unsafe blocks and 3 pub unsafe fns (sockaddr.rs:73 view_as, :197 try_init, :232 set_length). Socket wraps an OwnedFd (sys/unix.rs:940); raw fds enter only through unsafe FromRawFd (sys/unix.rs:3057) or the crate-private from_raw fed by syscalls (socket.rs:86). The sockaddr layout cast of RUSTSEC-2020-0079 is fixed since 0.3.16. No RustSec advisory affects 0.6.5. Maintenance: last released 2026-07-13, published by the rust-lang organization (repo rust-lang/socket2; owners sfackler, Thomasdezeeuw, rust-lang-owner, github:tokio-rs:socket2); license MIT OR Apache-2.0."
}
{
